{"question_id":"m9ekobbe","content":"<p>The correct statements from the following are :</p><p>(A) Tl<sup>3+</sup> is a powerful oxidising agent</p><p>(B) Al<sup>3+</sup> does not get reduced easily</p><p>(C) Both Al<sup>3+</sup> and Tl<sup>3+</sup> are very stable in solution</p><p>(D) Tl<sup>1+</sup> is more stable than Tl<sup>3+</sup></p><p>(E) Al<sup>3+</sup> and Tl<sup>1+</sup> are highly stable</p><p>Choose the <b>correct</b> answer from the options given below :</p>","chapter":"p-block-elements","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","isBonus":false,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2025-online-7th-april-evening-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2025 (Online) 7th April Evening Shift","permalink":"pthe-correct-statements-from-the-following-are-ppa-jee-main-chemistry-jtexf3qyj0i5q7mx","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>The correct statements from the following are :</p><p>(A) Tl<sup>3+</sup> is a powerful oxidising agent</p><p>(B) Al<sup>3+</sup> does not get reduced easily</p><p>(C) Both Al<sup>3+</sup> and Tl<sup>3+</sup> are very stable in solution</p><p>(D) Tl<sup>1+</sup> is more stable than Tl<sup>3+</sup></p><p>(E) Al<sup>3+</sup> and Tl<sup>1+</sup> are highly stable</p><p>Choose the <b>correct</b> answer from the options given below :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<p>(A), (B), (D) and (E) only</p>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"<p>(A), (C) and (D) only</p>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"<p>(A), (B), (C) and (E)</p>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"<p>(B), (D) and (E) only</p>"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>(i) True: Tl<sup>1+</sup> is more stable than Tl<sup>3+</sup> due to the inert pair effect. Therefore, Tl<sup>3+</sup> acts as a powerful oxidizing agent.</p>\n<p>(ii) True: The standard reduction potential for Al<sup>3+/Al</sup> is -1.66 V, indicating that Al<sup>3+</sup> is difficult to reduce and thus highly stable.</p>\n<p>(iii) False: Tl<sup>3+</sup> is not stable in solution.</p>\n<p>(iv) True: Tl<sup>1+</sup> is more stable than Tl<sup>3+</sup>.</p>\n<p>(v) True: Both Al<sup>3+</sup> and Tl<sup>1+</sup> are highly stable in their respective oxidation states.</p>"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>\u0928\u093f\u092e\u094d\u0928\u0932\u093f\u0916\u093f\u0924 \u092e\u0947\u0902 \u0938\u0947 \u0938\u0939\u0940 \u0915\u0925\u0928 \u0939\u0948\u0902 :</p>\n<p>(A) <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.495ex\" height=\"2.016ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -891.3 1986.7 891.3\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"54\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-54\"></use><use data-c=\"6C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6C\" transform=\"translate(722,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(1033,421.1) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u090f\u0915 \u0936\u0915\u094d\u0924\u093f\u0936\u093e\u0932\u0940 \u0911\u0915\u094d\u0938\u0940\u0915\u0930\u0923 \u0915\u0930\u094d\u092e\u0915 \u0939\u0948\u0964</p>\n<p>(B) <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.558ex\" height=\"2.066ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -913.3 2014.7 913.3\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/